/-!
# Stacks 085D (1) under generation in degree one of the algebra on the algebraic space

In Situation 0849 the graded algebra `𝒜` is a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_X`-algebra on the small
étale site of the algebraic space `X`. Stacks 085D supposes that **`𝒜` is generated as an
`𝒜₀`-algebra by `𝒜₁`**. For a quasi-coherent graded algebra this is a condition on the sections
over the affine objects of the small étale site: over every étale chart `V ⟶ X` with affine
`V`, the ring `⨁ₙ 𝒜ₙ(V)` is generated by `𝒜₁(V)` over `𝒜₀(V)`, that is, every section of
`𝒜_{1+n}(V)` is a sum of products of a section of `𝒜₁(V)` with one of `𝒜ₙ(V)`. This file
states that condition on `𝒜` itself,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`, in the form of
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` (the sheaf-level predicate of the case of
projective bundles) at the affine objects
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.affineObjects`, and deduces from it the hypothesis
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjIsoF1`: for every étale chart
`u : U ⟶ X`, the restriction `u^*𝒜` is generated in degree one over every affine open of `U`.

## The argument

For an étale chart `u : U ⟶ X` the restriction `u^*𝒜` is the pullback of sheaves of graded
algebras along `u` (Stacks 0FQX) read on the Zariski opens of `U`. A Zariski open `O ⊆ U` is an
étale chart `W` of the represented space `U`, whose composite with `u` is an étale chart `u W`
of `X` with the same underlying scheme `O`; it is affine when `O` is.

* **Sections.** In each degree the pullback of modules along the étale `u` is étale
  restriction (Stacks 03LW, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullbackIsoEtaleModulePullback`), so
  the sections of `u^*𝒜ₖ` over `W` are identified with those of `𝒜ₖ` over `u W`.
* **Products.** The identification is inverse to the map
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.gradedPullPostcompSection`: the unit `𝒜 ⟶ u_* u^*𝒜` of the graded
  adjunction of Stacks 0FQX, followed by the reading of a section of a direct image over `u W`
  at `W`, through the chart `W ×_X U` of `U` over `u W`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.postcompChartSection`). The unit is a homomorphism of graded
  algebras, and the reading is natural in the sheaf of sets, hence multiplicative on a direct
  image of a graded algebra (`Stacks.Sheaves.GradedAlgebraEssentiallySmall.natural_family_mul`).
  That they are inverse is the triangle identity of postcomposition against base change of étale
  charts, after `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSetProj_etaleModulePullbackAdjunction_unit`.
* So the sections of `u^*𝒜` over `W` are a copy of those of `𝒜` over `u W`, degreewise and
  multiplicatively, and generation in degree one passes across
  (`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.isGeneratedInDegreeOne_of_bijective`); likewise across the
  re-presentation of `𝒜` with sections in the universe of the site
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.smallAlgebraEquiv`). Over an affine open the
  degree-by-degree condition is the generation of the ring of sections as an algebra
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.adjoin_grading_one_eq_top`).

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`: `𝒜` is generated as an
  `𝒜₀`-algebra by `𝒜₁`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjIsoF1OfGenerated`: **Stacks 085D,
  part (1)**, `P ≅ F₁` for the constructed `P = Proj_X(𝒜)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isGeneratedInDegreeOne_gradedPull`: generation in degree one passes
  to the pullback along an étale representable morphism, chart by chart.
* `Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne.isGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts`: the
  hypothesis on `𝒜` gives the hypothesis on its restrictions to the étale charts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 085D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FQX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FQX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03LW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03LW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
-/

